---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Latch Tools"
  description="Latch Tools processes all files locally in your browser. No uploads and no cookies; the only analytics is a cookieless page-load count. Read the full policy."
  ogImage="/og/privacy-policy.png"
>
  <Header />

  <main>
    <section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 0">
      <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 780px">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="bar"></span>Legal</span>
        <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.06; font-size: clamp(30px, 4.5vw, 44px); margin: 18px 0 0;">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p style="color: var(--text-3); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 40px;">
          Last updated: 19 November 2026
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
      <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 680px">
        <div class="prose">

          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <p>
            Latch converts and processes your files entirely inside your browser.
            No file — not a single byte of its content — is ever sent to our servers
            or any third party. We cannot access your files, and we do not try to.
          </p>

          <h2>What we do <em>not</em> collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Your files or any part of their content.</li>
            <li>Filenames, file sizes, or metadata about files you process.</li>
            <li>Conversion results or downloads.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            All processing happens using your device's own CPU and browser APIs
            (Canvas, WebAssembly, JavaScript). The results are created locally and
            downloaded directly to your device.
          </p>

          <h2>What Cloudflare Pages collects</h2>
          <p>
            Latch is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. When you visit the site, Cloudflare's
            infrastructure records standard server access data: your IP address,
            user-agent string, the page requested, and the timestamp. This is typical
            of any web server and is not specific to Latch.
          </p>
          <p>
            These logs are used for security, abuse prevention, and uptime monitoring.
            They are not linked to individuals, not sold, and not used for advertising.
            See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-text)">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a> for details.
          </p>

          <h2>Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            Latch uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page loads and see how fast
            pages load. Cloudflare adds a small script to each page
            (<code>static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js</code>), and when you
            leave a page it sends one report to <code>latchtools.com/cdn-cgi/rum</code>.
            That report contains:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>the address of the page, and the page you came from, if any;</li>
            <li>your browser engine and version, and your operating system version;</li>
            <li>load timings, such as time to first byte and how long the page took to draw;</li>
            <li>a random ID for that one page load, made fresh every time.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            It contains nothing about the files you open, their names or sizes, or
            anything you type or draw in a tool. Latch never puts any of that in a page
            address, so the address can't carry it either. The script sets no cookies
            and stores nothing in your browser, so it has no way to link one visit
            to the next. We see totals in Cloudflare's dashboard, such as visits per page,
            countries and browsers, not individual visitors. If your browser or a
            content blocker blocks the script, every tool works the same.
          </p>

          <h2>Third-party scripts</h2>
          <p>
            The Cloudflare Web Analytics script above is the only script on the site
            that Latch didn't write. Fonts and every library the tools use are served
            from latchtools.com itself, so no font service or code CDN is contacted, and
            there is no advertising or tracking script. When you first use a tool it may
            fetch more of Latch's own code from latchtools.com, such as the PDF reader or
            an image codec, but nothing is ever sent back. You can watch this in your
            browser's network panel.
          </p>

          <h2>Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            Latch sets no cookies, and neither does the analytics script, so no consent
            banner is shown. If cookies are ever needed, for advertising or anything
            else, this policy will change before they are set, and visitors in the UK
            and EU will be asked first.
          </p>

          <h2>Your rights (UK &amp; EU)</h2>
          <p>
            Latch holds no personal data about you. The analytics reports carry no
            identifier that lasts beyond one page load, and the server logs above are
            kept by Cloudflare, not by us, so there is nothing for us to look up,
            correct or erase. If you have questions, contact us at the address below.
          </p>

          <h2>Children</h2>
          <p>
            Latch is a general-purpose utility and does not knowingly collect data from
            children under 13 (or the relevant age of digital consent in your jurisdiction).
          </p>

          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            If this policy changes in a meaningful way, for example if ads are
            introduced, the "last updated" date at the top will change and
            we will describe what is new. Continued use of the site after a material
            change constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions or concerns about this policy:
            <a href="mailto:privacy@latchtools.com" style="color: var(--accent-text)">privacy@latchtools.com</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 20px;
    letter-spacing: -.02em;
    margin: 44px 0 12px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .prose h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .prose p {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .prose ul {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .prose ul li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .prose em { font-style: italic; }
  .prose code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .9em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
